WEBVTT

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:03.860
According to the transmission,

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.230
it seems the No. 1 and No. 2 
Divisions have joined forces.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.300
I see.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.710
Apparently it was worth all the trouble

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.700
Shichisei went through trying to mix both 
Japanese and Americans in those divisions.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.860
Yes.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:16.820
However...

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.080
What is it?

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.070
Since we received that transmission

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:27.000
we have not received another 
transmission from Mars.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.800
<i>Prime Minister Hiruma, 
President Goodman is on the hotline.</i>

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.270
All right.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.770
Inform Shichisei about that matter.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:40.800
Yes, sir.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.660
Hello, Gerald.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:06.870
Hello there, Ichiro.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.880
I'm sure you can guess, but its an 
invitation to the summit meeting.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.610
You probably know what the topic will be.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.670
However, Ichiro, as the 
head of an allied nation,

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.520
let me tell you this beforehand.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.870
Please listen carefully...

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.990
<b><i>This Way and That Way</i></b>

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:54.240
You're not going to throw it?

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:05.230
<i>Marcos is there... along with 
Kanako, Jared, and Erika.</i>

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.390
Hey, what about Kana-chan and the others?

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.720
Did they make it there okay?

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.390
Do you think we can get there soon, too?

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.010
Alex? Is everything okay?

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:19.870
Yeah. Kanako delivered Akari 
and the squad leader,

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.550
we got them the medicine, 
and we'll get there soon as well.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:31.670
Akari will protect Marcos and the others.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:34.990
<i>Sheila...</i>

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:39.200
Marcos.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:40.940
Y-Yeah?

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.740
Take care of the roaches around here.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:43.390
Right.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.560
Kanako, get the survivors to safety.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.800
Roger.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.980
Those hands... look like

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:55.730
a mole cricket's.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.400
<i>The mole cricket.</i>

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:04.970
<i>It climbs, swims, digs holes, 
runs, jumps, flies, and cries.</i>

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.840
<i>Its seven abilities are also 
called its seven talents.</i>

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.970
<i>Also, it has astonishing arm strength.</i>

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.840
What I'm about to do right now might be

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.570
considered taking out my anger on you,

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:20.190
and you might not understand why 
you're getting this beating...

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.220
But even though you can't 
understand me anyway,

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.480
I'm going to say this...

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.350
Come at me.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.220
<i>The rainbow stag beetle.</i>

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.180
<i>It has the hard shell that's 
characteristic of beetles,</i>

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.720
<i>and its iridescent color creates a camouflaging effect.</i>

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:11.790
Commander Davis!

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:15.210
Let me find it!

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.170
If we use my power—

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.860
Just rest, Jared.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.500
Please let me do this.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:27.260
I'm not very smart, so I don't 
understand international affairs.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:30.230
Not only that, I'm a drifter who kept 
doing stupid things and went broke,

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.840
and then somehow got lucky enough 
to undergo the operation...

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.820
But when I heard the details of 
this mission, I was very proud.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.090
Because we were going to be saving 
Earth from some unknown virus.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:42.030
That's why with these roaches 
getting in the way,

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.550
and even worse, a human, just like us,

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:48.910
trying to use the project that you and the 
captain are risking their lives for...

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.100
I don't want to lose, even if I die.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.480
You're right, Jared.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.220
I'm counting on you.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.950
I'm going to defeat it.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:22.520
Crap!

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:32.520
Alex...

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.400
I'm sorry!

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:51.760
Even though I was with her,

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:57.070
Sheila... Sheila was...

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.010
Marcos.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.810
Read the situation.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:30.410
I'll kill you.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.480
The reason I punched you is because you

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:42.260
looked like you wanted to get punched.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:47.340
What did we come all the way 
to Mars for, huh, Marcos?!

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.660
To protect Sheila—

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.560
Then there's no reason for 
you to apologize to me.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.310
I'm here for a different reason.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:01.400
Ever since we were born, 
we were on the side of people

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.210
who were just going to 
be used and thrown away.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:05.860
Our only choices were to join a 
gang, or sell ourselves.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:07.820
If we didn't do anything, 
we were just trash.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.700
I came here to change my lot in life!

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:12.670
Isn't that why you came here, too?

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:15.100
It's a fight to live a decent life!

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.610
There's no time for you to 
be crying with your face

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:20.030
against the ground on this planet full of roaches!

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.720
We're going to avenge her.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.280
We're going to complete this mission,

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.280
kill the roaches and the traitors, 
and then head back to Earth.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.650
That sums it up... Right,

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:41.310
Captain?

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.940
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.520
Alex, thanks.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.040
No problem.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.210
Our current battle,

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.070
as well as the upcoming battles...

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:07.050
We're not going to lose any of them.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:12.040
There are 39 more days until 
the rescue vessel arrives!

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:21.470
We're going to survive them,

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:24.300
no matter what!

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:30.650
Do it, Jared.

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:36.530
<i>Echolocation.</i>

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.410
<i>The special sense that 
killer whales and dolphins</i>

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:41.470
<i>use by emitting sound waves.</i>

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.420
I found it, Commander! It's right above—

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.790
Yeah, I heard it...

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:57.950
The bastard trying to sneak up
behind someone who's wounded.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.350
I heard it loud and clear!

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.430
I was born with exceptionally good ears.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.230
<i>This bastard is copying me...</i>

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.880
N-Not good. It's a stag beetle.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.410
You bastard. Let go of Michelle-san!

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:22.760
Why you...

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:51.900
On Earth, if you forcefully touch a girl, 
it's called sexual harassment.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:57.240
It leads to lawsuits, fines, pay 
cuts, dismissals, and sometimes...

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:02.910
Even this.

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:09.830
It can't be...

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.870
Sir, are you certain about this?

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:15.790
Yes, according to President Goodman.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:19.600
I cannot understand it at all.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.480
What's going to happen to Captain Komachi

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.470
and the rest of the crew that is on Mars?

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:29.500
Right now they are probably fighting, 
believing that help is on the way.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.480
And yet...

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:35.280
The rescue vessel from Plan Delta 
hasn't even taken off yet.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:56.500
Transmissions from Mars have ceased.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:01.530
Apparently every division's radio 
waves disappeared all at once.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.260
That doesn't mean they all died, but...

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.310
...there is an interference.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:17.510
But that couldn't be due to the 
intelligence of the cockroaches.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.320
Who could have...

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:24.880
Are you familiar with fighters and sneakers?

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.670
It's the behavior of insects, isn't it?

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:33.000
The ones who use their own strength to 
challenge others and win are fighters.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.340
The ones who don't fight and 
steal deviously are sneakers.

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:40.520
The general of the Annex 
1 project is an American.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:45.010
Under him are fourteen 
commanders, including myself.

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:47.350
Which means

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:48.710
what exactly?

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:52.730
That there are fighters 
and sneakers here, too.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.270
Th-This is...

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:12.860
Adolf-san...

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.400
Now, what will you do?

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:23.880
Your boss died.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:27.720
Shouldn't you fall back 
and think up a new plan?

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:33.230
Oh! Or could it be that you think 
 I'm the one who did this?

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:37.110
What? Seriously? Do you guys 
actually care about revenge?

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:41.240
Or is this more of a "whatever, 
kill 'em all" kind of approach?

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:45.750
I don't have the time to be 
dealing with you guys right now.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:51.000
Someone was showing the roaches this.

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:57.090
And that's how they knew 
to attack our storage.

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.690
They knew what the medicine meant, too.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.060
Division Leader,

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.020
about the escape vessel...

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:07.640
This has a fake landing location drawn on it.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.050
I see...

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:15.810
It has to be them.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:23.110
Roaches that are just black and 
hard are so yesterday.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:35.290
Akari?

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:45.970
Akari...

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:48.340
<i>Hey,</i>

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.350
<i>his fighting style is...</i>

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:52.470
<i>getting sloppy?</i>

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:55.140
Hey, Akari. What's wrong?

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.060
Hey! Akari!

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:07.970
Calm down, Akari.

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:10.850
Come back.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.950
You're not who you used to be.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.710
You're one of us now.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:25.870
Captain... Michelle-san.

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:34.180
That bastard!

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:36.810
I-It's fine, Michelle-san.

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:40.990
I've already caught it.

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:44.860
The net really is an amazing invention.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.710
It gets tangled up on its own.

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:51.020
A little while ago, I spread my string
 loosely out on the ground like a net.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.880
Right about now it's tangled in the strings,

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.880
and those strings got 
mixed in with the dirt

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:58.060
and should have turned into a bag.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:02.680
Like a bagworm that's so hard, 
even a bee or a praying mantis

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:04.500
can't open it.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.220
It'll never be surfacing ever again.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.740
Captain, thank you very much.

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:21.760
I used the medicine, and yet I 
ended up like that one time...

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:24.860
I haven't done anything.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:26.230
More importantly...

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:30.430
Don't act like this is all over. It's too early for that.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:32.710
Jeez. Apparently it's true when

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:35.240
they say that where there's 
one, there's thirty of them.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.970
I think that's actually a hundred...

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:41.480
Anyway, there's only one 
thing we have to do.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:19.790
Unlike the cunning sneakers they are...

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:24.040
We are fighting against them.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.370
While acting like an ally, 
only to try to steal

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:31.340
another's one moment of 
progress at a high price.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.170
Against those weaklings...

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:34.530
They will not lose.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:38.330
We will not let them have Hizamaru 
Akari, Michelle K. Davis,

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.570
or your research.

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:52.880
You will come with me, won't you?

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:19.420
Sushi...

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.100
Fatty tuna.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.570
Bluefin tuna.

00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:33.860
<i>Hey, Sheila.</i>

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:37.560
<i>We can't go to where you are just yet.</i>

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.740
<i>Because we have this battle</i>

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.700
<i>to deal with.</i>

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.730
<i>Komachi Shokichi...</i>

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:18.240
<i>He, along with the ones he has 
accepted as his comrades...</i>

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:23.280
<i>I will not abandon anyone ever again.</i>

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:30.750
<i>I, Hiruma Ichiro, will give all that I have</i>

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:34.760
<i>and save them, no matter what.</i>

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:23.040
What were you two talking about?

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.130
What are you doing, Sheila?!

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:25.130
Sheila!

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:30.580
You bastards don't seem to understand 
after hearing it the first time...

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.840
So I'll say it again,
 as many times as I need to.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.800
Even if you steal our equipment 
and technology and get stronger,

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.680
and even if there are some sneaky bastards

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.970
on the inside holding us back,

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:56.650
we won't lose, no matter what.

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.240
Don't underestimate

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.360
the Earth,

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:06.280
and the Earth's organisms!

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:52.930
The landmines are set.
